# ScrollBench Integration Walkthrough

I have integrated the "ScrollBench" test application into the main project build system. This ensures that when you pull the project, you can build both the Main App and ScrollBench using the standard [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1) script, without needing to configure them separately.

## Changes

### 1. Unified CMake Configuration
- **File:** [CMakeLists.txt](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/CMakeLists.txt)
- **Change:** Added `add_subdirectory(test_scrollbench)` to the root CMake file. This tells the build system to include the ScrollBench project as part of the main build.

### 2. Embeddable ScrollBench
- **File:** [test_scrollbench/CMakeLists.txt](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/CMakeLists.txt)
- **Change:** Modified the file to detect if it's being built standalone or as part of the main project.
    - If standalone: It sets up its own project and tools.
    - If integrated: It reuses the main project's configuration and libraries (like LibRaw), preventing conflicts.

### 3. Updated Build Script
- **File:** [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1)
- **Change:** 
    - Added a **Dependency Check** step at the very beginning. It verifies that critical FFmpeg DLLs exist before starting the build.
    - Updated the success report to check for and display the path to `appScrollBench.exe`.

### 4. Large File Storage (LFS)
- **Change:** The project now uses **Git LFS** to track [avcodec-62.dll](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/avcodec-62.dll) (which is >100MB).
- **Configuration:** Created `.gitattributes` to automatically handle this file.
- **Why:** This ensures the file can be synced to GitHub without hitting size limits, while still being available for the build system.

## Verification Results

### Automated Build Verification
I ran a full clean build using `.\build.ps1 -Clean`.

**Result:** SUCCESS
- The build verified 177 compilation targets.
- Both `appSamsungGallery` (Main App) and `appScrollBench` were linked successfully.

### Output Files
The following executables were generated:
- [build\appSamsungGallery.exe](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build/appSamsungGallery.exe)
- `build\test_scrollbench\appScrollBench.exe`

You can now develop both applications simultaneously. If you add new files to ScrollBench, they will be picked up by the main build automatically.
